title: The open presidential primary

@franchise
title: Who is the Left?
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.primary_biedron_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_zandberg_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_adb_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_zukowska_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_kotula_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_biejat_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_field_size = 0;
!}

= The primary franchise

An open contest resolves nothing until the alliance defines its electorate.
Every boundary creates a different Left: party delegates, organised members or
a public assembled by the candidates themselves.

- @delegates
- @members
- @supporters

@delegates
title: Limit the vote to founding-party delegates
subtitle: Cheap and controlled. The founders choose the field as well as the winner.
on-arrival: primary_electorate = "Founding-party delegates"; primary_franchise_code = 1; primary_turnout = 1400; barons_dissent -= 3; spring_dissent -= 2; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "Delegates receive the presidential ballots"
go-to: access

@members
title: Let members and affiliated movements vote
subtitle: Organised currents gain weight; no candidate can rely on television alone.
choose-if: razem_cooperation >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: Razem and movement organisers do not trust the common register.
on-arrival: primary_electorate = "Members and affiliated movements"; primary_franchise_code = 2; primary_turnout = 52000; organiser_energy += 2; movement_autonomy += 2; barons_dissent += 2; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The alliance opens one verified membership register"
go-to: access

@supporters
title: Register sympathisers for a public primary
subtitle: The broadest mandate, the widest field and the greatest capture risk.
choose-if: primary_signature_network or local_network >= 45 or turnout_readiness >= 61
unavailable-subtitle: No signature network or local register can verify a public electorate.
on-arrival: primary_electorate = "Registered sympathisers"; primary_franchise_code = 3; primary_turnout = 180000; public_trust += 3; turnout_readiness += 4; media_capacity += 2; barons_dissent += 5; movement_autonomy += 3; news_headline = "Registered sympathisers turn the nomination into a public contest"
go-to: access


@access
title: Who may stand?
new-page: true

= Ballot access

The electorate is **[+ primary_electorate +]**. The next rule decides whether
the ballot belongs to the founding organisations, rewards candidates who can
bridge currents, or can be opened by a supporter campaign.

- @founders
- @cross_current
- @petitions

@founders
title: Guarantee one place to each founding organisation
subtitle: Biedroń, Zandberg and one SLD nominee form a controlled three-person field.
on-arrival: primary_rules = "Founding-organisation nominations"; primary_access_code = 1; party_unity += 2; barons_dissent -= 2; progressives_dissent += 2; labor_dissent += 1; news_headline = "The founders protect three places on the ballot"
go-to: ballot

@cross_current
title: Require endorsements from two political currents
subtitle: Bridge candidates can qualify without owning a founding organisation.
choose-if: primary_cross_faction_pact or primary_rules_written or primary_franchise_code >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The currents never agreed how to recognise one another's endorsements.
on-arrival: primary_rules = "Two-current endorsement"; primary_access_code = 2; party_unity += 1; progressives_dissent -= 2; labor_dissent -= 2; barons_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Cross-current endorsements widen the primary"
go-to: ballot

@petitions
title: Use a low supporter-petition threshold
subtitle: All six campaigns may qualify; prepared movements gain more than headquarters.
choose-if: primary_franchise_code = 3 and (primary_signature_network or local_network >= 45)
unavailable-subtitle: Only a verified public electorate with a signature network can sustain petitions.
on-arrival: primary_rules = "Supporter-petition access"; primary_access_code = 3; party_unity -= 1; organiser_energy += 3; movement_autonomy += 4; barons_dissent += 5; news_headline = "Supporter petitions place six campaigns on the ballot"
go-to: ballot


@ballot
title: The qualified field
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const primaryBallotNumber = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};

const ballotLabor = primaryBallotNumber(Q.labor_strength, 0);
const ballotProgressives = primaryBallotNumber(Q.progressives_strength, 0);
const ballotBarons = primaryBallotNumber(Q.barons_strength, 0);
const ballotSpring = primaryBallotNumber(Q.spring_strength, 0);
const ballotRazem = primaryBallotNumber(Q.razem_strength, 0);
const ballotMedia = primaryBallotNumber(Q.media_capacity, 0);
const ballotPublicSector = primaryBallotNumber(Q.public_sector_support, 0);
const ballotLaborDissent = primaryBallotNumber(Q.labor_dissent, 0);
const ballotProgressiveDissent =
    primaryBallotNumber(Q.progressives_dissent, 0);

Q.primary_biedron_eligible = 1;
Q.primary_zandberg_eligible = 1;
Q.primary_adb_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_zukowska_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_kotula_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_biejat_eligible = 0;
Q.primary_sld_nominee = "None";

if (Q.primary_access_code == 1) {
    let adbNomination =
        ballotLabor * 0.8 + ballotProgressives * 0.35 +
        ballotPublicSector * 0.15 - ballotLaborDissent * 0.15;
    let zukowskaNomination =
        ballotBarons * 0.75 + ballotProgressives * 0.35 +
        ballotMedia * 0.12 - ballotProgressiveDissent * 0.12;

    if (
        Q.dziemianowicz_bak_advisor ||
        Q.primary_new_generation ||
        Q.primary_social_slate ||
        Q.primary_union_slate
    ) {
        adbNomination += 8;
    }
    if (
        Q.zukowska_advisor ||
        Q.primary_machine_slate ||
        Q.primary_spokesperson_slate
    ) {
        zukowskaNomination += 8;
    }

    if (adbNomination >= zukowskaNomination) {
        Q.primary_adb_eligible = 1;
        Q.primary_sld_nominee = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk";
    } else {
        Q.primary_zukowska_eligible = 1;
        Q.primary_sld_nominee = "Anna-Maria Żukowska";
    }
}

if (Q.primary_access_code == 2) {
    Q.primary_adb_eligible = 1;
    Q.primary_biejat_eligible = 1;

    Q.primary_zukowska_eligible =
        Q.zukowska_advisor ||
        Q.primary_machine_slate ||
        Q.primary_spokesperson_slate ||
        ballotBarons + ballotProgressives >= 30 ? 1 : 0;

    Q.primary_kotula_eligible =
        Q.kotula_advisor ||
        Q.primary_equality_slate ||
        Q.primary_movement_slate ||
        ballotSpring + ballotProgressives >= 30 ? 1 : 0;
}

if (Q.primary_access_code == 3) {
    Q.primary_adb_eligible = 1;
    Q.primary_zukowska_eligible = 1;
    Q.primary_kotula_eligible = 1;
    Q.primary_biejat_eligible = 1;
}

Q.primary_field_size =
    Q.primary_biedron_eligible +
    Q.primary_zandberg_eligible +
    Q.primary_adb_eligible +
    Q.primary_zukowska_eligible +
    Q.primary_kotula_eligible +
    Q.primary_biejat_eligible;
!}

= The ballot takes shape

Rules: **[+ primary_rules +]**  
Electorate: **[+ primary_electorate +]**

[? if primary_access_code = 1:
The founders reserve one place each. Wiosna nominates **Robert Biedroń**,
Razem nominates **Adrian Zandberg**, and the SLD contest produces
**[+ primary_sld_nominee +]**. ?]

[? if primary_access_code = 2:
Biedroń and Zandberg qualify through their organisations. Dziemianowicz-Bąk
and Biejat assemble endorsements across labour, progressive and municipal
currents; Żukowska and Kotula qualify only where their supporting structures
are strong enough. ?]

[? if primary_access_code = 3:
The petition threshold admits all six campaigns. Headquarters can no longer
prevent an organised candidate from reaching the voters. ?]

**Qualified candidates:**

[? if primary_biedron_eligible: - **Robert Biedroń** — Wiosna, media reach and a public-facing campaign. ?]
[? if primary_zandberg_eligible: - **Adrian Zandberg** — Razem, programme and organised economic-left support. ?]
[? if primary_adb_eligible: - **Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk** — labour-progressive crossover and public services. ?]
[? if primary_zukowska_eligible: - **Anna-Maria Żukowska** — SLD organisation, spokespeople and party delegates. ?]
[? if primary_kotula_eligible: - **Katarzyna Kotula** — equality movements, Wiosna activists and public mobilisation. ?]
[? if primary_biejat_eligible: - **Magdalena Biejat** — Razem, labour, tenants and municipal organising. ?]

- @campaign: Choose the campaign arena


@campaign
title: How will the primary be fought?
new-page: true

= The primary campaign

Ballot: **[+ primary_rules +]**  
Electorate: **[+ primary_electorate +]**  
Candidates: **[+ primary_field_size +]**

The arena cannot create a constituency that does not exist, but it decides
which constituency becomes visible on polling day.

- @television
- @counties
- @issues

@television
title: Hold three televised debates
subtitle: Best for Biedroń and Żukowska; Kotula can break through with movement energy.
choose-if: media_capacity >= 20 or primary_tv_ready
unavailable-subtitle: The alliance lacks the production and briefing capacity for national debates.
on-arrival: primary_campaign = "Televised debates"; primary_campaign_code = 1; media_capacity += 2; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Three debates turn the primary into national programming"
go-to: tally

@counties
title: Send the field through county hustings
subtitle: Best for Dziemianowicz-Bąk and Biejat; rewards regional crossover work.
choose-if: local_network >= 45 or primary_signature_network
unavailable-subtitle: Too few county organisations can host and verify the ballot.
on-arrival: primary_campaign = "County hustings"; primary_campaign_code = 2; local_network += 2; turnout_readiness += 2; news_headline = "County hustings test who can organise beyond Warsaw"
go-to: tally

@issues
title: Use workplace, tenant and equality forums
subtitle: Best for programme candidates; Zandberg, Biejat, Kotula and Dziemianowicz-Bąk all have a route.
on-arrival: primary_campaign = "Workplace, tenant and equality forums"; primary_campaign_code = 3; labor_credibility += 1; feminist_trust += 1; organiser_energy += 1; news_headline = "Issue forums make the primary argue about power"
go-to: tally


@tally
title: Count the primary
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const primaryNumber = function(value, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(value)) ? Number(value) : fallback;
};

const springStrength = primaryNumber(Q.spring_strength, 0);
const razemStrength = primaryNumber(Q.razem_strength, 0);
const laborStrength = primaryNumber(Q.labor_strength, 0);
const progressiveStrength = primaryNumber(Q.progressives_strength, 0);
const baronsStrength = primaryNumber(Q.barons_strength, 0);

const springDissent = primaryNumber(Q.spring_dissent, 0);
const razemDissent = primaryNumber(Q.razem_dissent, 0);
const laborDissent = primaryNumber(Q.labor_dissent, 0);
const progressiveDissent = primaryNumber(Q.progressives_dissent, 0);

const mediaCapacity = primaryNumber(Q.media_capacity, 0);
const womenSupport = primaryNumber(Q.women_support, 0);
const workersSupport = primaryNumber(Q.workers_support, 0);
const laborCredibility = primaryNumber(Q.labor_credibility, 0);
const publicSectorSupport = primaryNumber(Q.public_sector_support, 0);
const youngSupport = primaryNumber(Q.young_support, 0);
const feministTrust = primaryNumber(Q.feminist_trust, 0);
const householdSecurity = primaryNumber(Q.household_security, 0);
const organiserEnergy = primaryNumber(Q.organiser_energy, 0);

let biedron =
    18 + springStrength * 0.40 - springDissent * 0.14 +
    mediaCapacity * 0.08 + womenSupport * 0.03;

let zandberg =
    17 + razemStrength * 0.42 - razemDissent * 0.14 +
    laborCredibility * 0.09 + workersSupport * 0.04;

let adb =
    15 + laborStrength * 0.27 + progressiveStrength * 0.25 -
    (laborDissent + progressiveDissent) * 0.075 +
    publicSectorSupport * 0.07 + womenSupport * 0.02;

let zukowska =
    14 + progressiveStrength * 0.25 + baronsStrength * 0.21 -
    progressiveDissent * 0.10 + mediaCapacity * 0.07 +
    youngSupport * 0.02;

let kotula =
    13 + progressiveStrength * 0.22 + springStrength * 0.22 -
    (progressiveDissent + springDissent) * 0.065 +
    feministTrust * 0.09 + youngSupport * 0.03;

let biejat =
    14 + razemStrength * 0.25 + laborStrength * 0.25 -
    (razemDissent + laborDissent) * 0.065 +
    householdSecurity * 0.05 + organiserEnergy * 0.06;

// The franchise decides which organisations can mobilise voters.
if (Q.primary_franchise_code == 1) {
    biedron += 5; zandberg += 3; adb += 4;
    zukowska += 9; kotula -= 3; biejat -= 2;
}
if (Q.primary_franchise_code == 2) {
    biedron += 3; zandberg += 7; adb += 7;
    zukowska += 4; kotula += 5; biejat += 7;
}
if (Q.primary_franchise_code == 3) {
    biedron += 8; zandberg += 2; adb += 5;
    zukowska += 4; kotula += 8; biejat += 6;
}

// Ballot access rewards the candidates who fit the qualifying rule.
if (Q.primary_access_code == 1) {
    biedron += 7; zandberg += 7; adb += 5;
    zukowska += 7; kotula -= 8; biejat -= 8;
}
if (Q.primary_access_code == 2) {
    biedron += 1; zandberg += 1; adb += 8;
    zukowska += 4; kotula += 7; biejat += 8;
}
if (Q.primary_access_code == 3) {
    biedron += 4; zandberg += 2; adb += 5;
    zukowska += 3; kotula += 10; biejat += 8;
}

// Campaign format converts different kinds of support into turnout.
if (Q.primary_campaign_code == 1) {
    biedron += 10; zandberg += 4; adb += 5;
    zukowska += 9; kotula += 7; biejat += 3;
}
if (Q.primary_campaign_code == 2) {
    biedron += 3; zandberg += 4; adb += 9;
    zukowska += 6; kotula += 6; biejat += 9;
}
if (Q.primary_campaign_code == 3) {
    biedron += 2; zandberg += 8; adb += 9;
    zukowska += 2; kotula += 10; biejat += 10;
}

// Earlier slates and advisers matter without being required for basic access.
if (Q.dziemianowicz_bak_advisor) adb += 3;
if (Q.primary_new_generation) adb += 4;
if (Q.primary_social_slate) adb += 4;
if (Q.primary_union_slate) {
    adb += 3;
    biejat += 3;
}

if (Q.zukowska_advisor) zukowska += 3;
if (Q.primary_machine_slate) zukowska += 5;
if (Q.primary_spokesperson_slate) zukowska += 4;

if (Q.kotula_advisor) kotula += 3;
if (Q.primary_equality_slate) kotula += 5;
if (Q.primary_movement_slate) {
    kotula += 4;
    biejat += 3;
}

if (Q.biejat_advisor) biejat += 3;
if (Q.primary_tenant_slate) biejat += 5;

// Similar candidates divide an organisational reservoir instead of creating
// additional voters from nowhere.
if (Q.primary_kotula_eligible) biedron -= 3;
if (Q.primary_biejat_eligible) zandberg -= 3;
if (Q.primary_adb_eligible && Q.primary_zukowska_eligible) {
    adb -= 1.5;
    zukowska -= 1.5;
}

Q.primary_biedron_weight = Q.primary_biedron_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(biedron)) : 0;
Q.primary_zandberg_weight = Q.primary_zandberg_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(zandberg)) : 0;
Q.primary_adb_weight = Q.primary_adb_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(adb)) : 0;
Q.primary_zukowska_weight = Q.primary_zukowska_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(zukowska)) : 0;
Q.primary_kotula_weight = Q.primary_kotula_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(kotula)) : 0;
Q.primary_biejat_weight = Q.primary_biejat_eligible
    ? Math.max(1, Math.round(biejat)) : 0;

const candidates = [
    ["Robert Biedroń", "biedron", Q.primary_biedron_weight],
    ["Adrian Zandberg", "zandberg", Q.primary_zandberg_weight],
    ["Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk", "adb", Q.primary_adb_weight],
    ["Anna-Maria Żukowska", "zukowska", Q.primary_zukowska_weight],
    ["Katarzyna Kotula", "kotula", Q.primary_kotula_weight],
    ["Magdalena Biejat", "biejat", Q.primary_biejat_weight]
].filter(function(candidate) {
    return candidate[2] > 0;
});

Q.primary_total_weight = candidates.reduce(function(total, candidate) {
    return total + candidate[2];
}, 0);

// Delegates are predictable; a public primary permits a little more turnout
// variation. The rules remain much more important than the random factor.
const primaryVariance =
    Q.primary_franchise_code == 3
        ? 0.08
        : (Q.primary_franchise_code == 2 ? 0.06 : 0.04);

const adjusted = candidates.map(function(candidate) {
    const turnoutFactor =
        1 - primaryVariance +
        this.random.uint32() / 4294967296 * primaryVariance * 2;
    return [
        candidate[0],
        candidate[1],
        candidate[2],
        candidate[2] * turnoutFactor
    ];
}.bind(this));

const adjustedTotal = adjusted.reduce(function(total, candidate) {
    return total + candidate[3];
}, 0);

let allocatedVotes = 0;
const tallied = adjusted.map(function(candidate, index) {
    const votes = index == adjusted.length - 1
        ? Math.max(0, Math.round(Q.primary_turnout) - allocatedVotes)
        : Math.max(
            0,
            Math.floor(
                Math.round(Q.primary_turnout) *
                candidate[3] /
                Math.max(1, adjustedTotal)
            )
        );

    allocatedVotes += votes;
    Q["primary_" + candidate[1] + "_tally"] = votes;
    return [candidate[0], candidate[1], candidate[2], votes];
});

Q.primary_total_votes = tallied.reduce(function(total, candidate) {
    return total + candidate[3];
}, 0);

tallied.forEach(function(candidate) {
    Q["primary_" + candidate[1] + "_share"] =
        Math.round(
            candidate[3] * 1000 /
            Math.max(1, Q.primary_total_votes)
        ) / 10;
});

const ordered = tallied.slice().sort(function(left, right) {
    if (right[3] != left[3]) return right[3] - left[3];
    if (right[2] != left[2]) return right[2] - left[2];
    return left[0] < right[0] ? -1 : 1;
});

const winner = ordered[0];
const runner = ordered[1];

Q.primary_winner = winner[0];
Q.primary_runner_up = runner ? runner[0] : "None";
Q.primary_winner_share =
    Q["primary_" + winner[1] + "_share"];
Q.primary_runner_share = runner
    ? Q["primary_" + runner[1] + "_share"]
    : 0;
Q.primary_margin =
    Math.round(
        (Q.primary_winner_share - Q.primary_runner_share) * 10
    ) / 10;
Q.primary_mandate = Math.round(Q.primary_winner_share);

if (Q.primary_winner_share >= 40 || Q.primary_margin >= 10) {
    Q.party_unity += 2;
} else if (
    Q.primary_winner_share < 25 ||
    Q.primary_margin < 2
) {
    Q.party_unity -= 2;
}
!}
go-to: result_biedron if primary_winner = "Robert Biedroń"; result_zandberg if primary_winner = "Adrian Zandberg"; result_adb if primary_winner = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk"; result_zukowska if primary_winner = "Anna-Maria Żukowska"; result_kotula if primary_winner = "Katarzyna Kotula"; result_biejat if primary_winner = "Magdalena Biejat"


@result_biedron
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Robert Biedroń"; presidential_candidate_base = 2.2; primary_active = 0; spring_dissent -= 9; spring_strength += 3; media_capacity += 3; razem_dissent += 4; barons_dissent += 2; news_headline = "Biedroń wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_zandberg
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg"; presidential_candidate_base = 3.2; primary_active = 0; razem_dissent -= 10; razem_strength += 3; labor_credibility += 4; spring_dissent += 6; barons_dissent += 5; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "Zandberg wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_adb
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk"; presidential_candidate_base = 3.0; primary_active = 0; labor_dissent -= 6; progressives_dissent -= 6; labor_credibility += 3; progressive_credibility += 3; public_sector_support += 2; women_support += 2; barons_dissent += 4; spring_dissent += 2; party_unity += 2; news_headline = "Dziemianowicz-Bąk wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_zukowska
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Anna-Maria Żukowska"; presidential_candidate_base = 2.6; primary_active = 0; progressives_dissent -= 6; barons_dissent -= 2; media_capacity += 4; young_support += 2; spring_dissent += 3; razem_dissent += 4; party_unity += 1; news_headline = "Żukowska wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_kotula
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Katarzyna Kotula"; presidential_candidate_base = 2.5; primary_active = 0; spring_dissent -= 6; progressives_dissent -= 5; feminist_trust += 5; women_support += 3; young_support += 3; barons_dissent += 6; razem_dissent += 2; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "Kotula wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result

@result_biejat
on-arrival: presidential_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat"; presidential_candidate_base = 2.7; primary_active = 0; razem_dissent -= 8; labor_dissent -= 4; organiser_energy += 3; labor_credibility += 3; household_policy_pressure += 2; barons_dissent += 6; spring_dissent += 3; party_unity -= 1; last_policy_stage = "Primary programme"; last_policy_authority = "Lewica party electorate"; last_policy_implementation = "Not enacted"; news_headline = "Biejat wins the open Left primary"
go-to: result


@result
title: A candidate with a constituency
new-page: true

= [+ presidential_candidate +] wins

**[+ presidential_candidate +]** wins **[+ primary_winner_share +]%** of the
counted primary vote. **[+ primary_runner_up +]** finishes second on
**[+ primary_runner_share +]%**, a margin of **[+ primary_margin +]** points.

Electorate: **[+ primary_electorate +]**  
Ballot access: **[+ primary_rules +]**  
Campaign: **[+ primary_campaign +]**

[? if primary_winner_share >= 40:
The winner has both a constituency and a broad primary mandate. Losing
organisations can dispute the programme, but not the result. ?]

[? if primary_winner_share < 40 and primary_margin >= 5:
The winner has a clear plurality rather than ownership of the whole alliance.
The nomination is settled; the coalition around it still has to be built. ?]

[? if primary_margin < 5:
The ballot settles the nomination by a narrow margin. The losing campaigns
retain enough organisation to demand programme, staff and campaign concessions.
?]

The rules chosen by the alliance created the electorate that has now created
its candidate. Every losing organisation retains a record of precisely which
boundary, access rule and campaign arena defeated it.

- @poland_events_2021_2023.independence_2019: Begin the presidential campaign
